face.rs`, `mcp_schema_tests.rs`, `mcp_compat_tests.rs` — instrumentation + contract tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — CLI regression report.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/**` — baseline + benchmark suites.\n- `extension/src/review/**` — Phase 10 review UI.\n- `extension/src/test/**` — extension UI smoke + contract tests.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-*.md` — design notes per phase.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-*.md` — operator + migration + benchmark + UI guides + runbook + recovery playbook.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R*.md` — all review outputs.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Where the per-task briefs live\n\nEvery task (`Txx`) and every review (`Rxx`) has a markdown file under [`tasks/`](tasks/) with: goal, prerequisites, inputs, steps, files-expected, verification commands, coding-standard checks, and definition-of-done for that task. Executors should open the next pending task's file before touching code.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:305:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BJaFo2nHFRQotGsvtzXBvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing markdown task brief files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files at the exact paths I name.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ IT FIRST — Phases 0 and 1 sections)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json  (READ IT FIRST — extract title, depends_on, files_expected, verification_commands for each task you write)\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md  (read the \"Hard limits\" and \"No broken windows\" sections)\n\nWrite these 11 files, each at the path `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT01, T02, T03, T04, R05, T06, T07, T08, T09, R10\n\n**Use this exact template structure (markdown) for each task file:**\n\n```\n# <TASK_ID> — <Title from tasks.json>\n\n**Phase:** <0 or 1>\n**Type:** <task_type from tasks.json>\n**Model class:** <model_class from tasks.json>\n**Depends on:** <depends_on list, comma-separated, or \"none\">\n**Spec anchor:** [§<Spec section name>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<lowercase-dashed-anchor>)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\n3–5 sentences. State what this task produces and why it matters for the substrate. Reference the spec's non-negotiables that apply.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> Direct quotes from the spec sections that bind this task (1-3 short quotes).\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: list the prior tasks' artifacts you read first.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on (cite exact paths under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/` or `extension/src/`).\n- Standards files to honor: coding.md hard limits, AGENTS.md backward compatibility rules.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. ... concrete step\n2. ... concrete step\n3. ... etc. 5-10 steps each. Be specific about file edits, table schema, function signatures where the spec is explicit.\n\n## Files expected\n\nFor each path in tasks.json `files_expected`:\n- `path/to/file.ext` — one-line purpose.\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command from tasks.json `verification_commands` verbatim. Add a sentence under each explaining what passing means.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l <new files>`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming.\n- For schema changes: schema parity (every column has a corresponding field; nullability matches).\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Heading` from the spec or architecture doc that authorizes any non-obvious choice (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §<this phase> punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n```\n\n**For review files (R05, R10), use this template instead:**\n\n```\n# <REVIEW_ID> — <Title from tasks.json>\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase <N>\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** <list>\n**Spec anchor:** [§<phase section>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<anchor>)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n\n## Purpose\n\nWhat this review certifies. 2-3 sentences.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by the listed dependency tasks.\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy.\n- Shared standards: coding.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to this phase.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. ... step\n2. ... step\n... be specific about what to grep for, what tests to re-run, what schema columns to spot-check.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/<REVIEW_ID>-<slug>.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits.\n- `## P99 budget evidence` (only for phases that have a P99 SLA in the spec).\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity, suggested follow-up tasks (do NOT defer outside this build).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command from tasks.json verbatim with a sentence explaining what passing means.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n```\n\n**Task-specific content guidance:**\n\n- T01 produces `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md`. The decision considers the four gate conditions in spec §Phase 0 (breaking memories table changes, identity primary-key changes, event log requiring incompatible WAL changes, two-or-more of the above). The decision MUST document evidence and a branch-or-repo name.\n- T02 produces architecture overview (workspace graph, event log, memory graph sections required) + MCP compatibility policy (backward compatibility required).\n- T03 names new crates `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, `lattice-verification` (live under daemon/crates/) OR documents why they're modules in `lattice-core` instead. Storage migration policy must include migration order and rollback.\n- T04 captures baseline benchmarks of EXISTING workflows so Phase 4/9 has something to regress against. Bench file uses criterion conventions.\n- T06–T09 implement the unified identity model from spec §Phase 1: stable IDs for files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, context handles; identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics; serialization in MCP payloads; legacy name compat. P99 budget ≤2ms.\n- R05 reviews Phase 0; R10 reviews Phase 1 (must include \"P99 budget evidence\" section).\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact spec section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 11 files. Then report a one-line confirmation per file with `ls -la` style output. Do NOT modify tasks.json. Do NOT modify context.md or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4404,"cache_read_input_tokens":124894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4404},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"c31b2af9-974b-46af-9b3a-d839c18c2ebe","request_id":"req_011Cb7MVwhDZjFqnUfLkL1CZ"}
