docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:359:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BJaFo2nHFRQotGsvtzXBvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing markdown task brief files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ Phases 4 and 5 sections + §Retrieval Engine + §Working Memory)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md\n\nWrite these 12 files at `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT27, T28, T29, T30, T31, T32, R33, T34, T35, T36, T37, R38\n\n**Use the same template structure as the prior agents** (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done) for work tasks; for review tasks use the review template with required headings.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T27 — intent classifier: classify user task by type (debug/refactor/explain/add-feature/test/docs/migration/etc.). Should be feature-based and inspectable per spec §Ranking Complexity risk.\n- T28 — anchor extractor: extract paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys; resolve into graph identities using identity resolver from Phase 1.\n- T29 — hybrid candidate retrieval: exact path/symbol lookup + code graph traversal + doc backlinks/outgoing links + FTS + embeddings + event similarity + memory links + workflow similarity + recent working memory.\n- T30 — scoring with ALL signals from spec §Retrieval Engine \"Ranking signals\": task-type compatibility, graph proximity, exact identifier match, semantic similarity, verification status, freshness, scope, evidence strength, contradiction/supersession state, past usefulness, recent successful reuse, user preference compatibility, token cost. Diagnostic mode exposes scores AND reasons.\n- T31 — compact response shaper: every result has an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`. Forward-compatible with Phase 5 working memory checkpoints per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint.\n- T32 — benchmark suite + golden anchors + ranking regression tests.\n- R33 — Phase 4 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T34 — working memory state from spec §Working Memory: task statement, interpreted intent, active files/symbols, active hypotheses, active failures, current plan, selected memories, excluded memories and reasons, budget decisions, unresolved questions, verification status. Table: `working_memory_checkpoints`.\n- T35 — operations: retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint.\n- T36 — MCP tool for inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons (`MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2).\n- T37 — tests: budgets, pinned context, eviction, checkpoint restore.\n- R38 — Phase 5 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nFor each task, include 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths (from tasks.json `files_expected`), and the exact verification commands from tasks.json. The \"Coding-standard checks\" section should include: file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for SQL tasks, n