./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:838:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DJMqeMGbDfRSjsJXmwYv1Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RpZgtYJJV9VcCeSHeieg1w","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R25.md","content":"# R25 — Backend review — Phase 3 memory graph storage\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase 3\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T19, T20, T21, T22, T23, T24\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-3-memory-graph-storage)\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review certifies that the Phase 3 memory graph substrate satisfies every spec invariant before retrieval (Phase 4) starts depending on it. It confirms: the schema covers all 13 memory classes (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class record); links, evidence, accesses, and scores are first-class tables; stream classification and scope enforcement deny-by-default work as specified; the legacy migration imports cleanly and idempotently; CRUD plus the full verification-status state machine emits the right events; contradiction, supersession, stale state, and replay all behave correctly. The verdict gates R26 (contract gate) and Phase 4.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from T19–T24:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/mod.rs`, `classes.rs`, `schema.sql`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/links.rs`, `evidence.rs`, `accesses.rs`, `scores.rs`, `links_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/streams.rs`, `scope.rs`, `scope_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/migration.rs`, `migration_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store.rs`, `transitions.rs`, `store_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/contradiction_tests.rs`, `supersession_tests.rs`, `replay_tests.rs`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-migration-guide.md`\n- Spec sections claimed satisfied:\n  - §Memory Graph (classes including CounterMemory, required fields, link types)\n  - §ViLoMem (typed streams)\n  - §Storage Design (memories, memory_links, memory_evidence, memory_accesses, memory_scores, indexes)\n  - §Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage (Deliverables + DoD)\n  - §Risks \"Scope Leakage\" and the deny-by-default control\n- Standards relevant to this phase: Cadres coding standard §Schema / model parity, §Error handling, §Naming, §No broken windows; Lattice CLAUDE.md on Markdown heading references.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Confirm `MemoryClass` enumerates all 13 spec variants and `CounterMemory` is present.\n2. Confirm `MemoryRecord` has one field per spec-required attribute; cross-check the schema column inventory against the spec list.\n3. Confirm the four first-class tables exist (`memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses`, `memory_scores`) with the columns and indexes from spec §Storage Design.\n4. Confirm `MemoryLinkType` enumerates all 11 spec variants; exhaustive `match` is used at write/read sites.\n5. Confirm `MemoryStream` enumerates the seven streams and `classify_stream` is total over `MemoryClass`.\n6. Confirm `ScopeFilter` is required on every read API (compile-time enforcement preferred; runtime `Underspecified` if not); confirm cross-scope leakage negative tests exist and pass.\n7. Confirm the migration importer is idempotent, dry-runnable, restartable, and that every legacy column has a documented destination in the migration-guide column-mapping table.\n8. Confirm the verification-status state machine matches the spec list and that disallowed transitions return typed errors.\n9. Confirm contradiction tests exercise both the `Contradicts` link path AND the `CounterMemory` first-class-record path, and that the two are observably distinct (CounterMemory has its own id, evidence, scope, and verification status).\n10. Confirm supersession chains preserve historical lookup and reject cycles.\n11. Confirm replay tests show byte-equivalence between full replay and snapshot + tail, and that corruption returns a typed error without silent recovery.\n12. Run the verification commands from tasks.json for T19–T24 from the repo root.\n13. Audit for coding-standard regressions: file lengths, function lengths, error-swallowing, raw-SQL interpolation, missing tracing on transitions.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\n`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` with these mandatory headings:\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — table mapping each Phase 3 deliverable + DoD line to the artifact that satisfies it.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — file-length, function-length, error-handling, schema-parity, SQL-binding, tracing audit results.\n- `## CounterMemory coverage` — explicit confirmation that `CounterMemory` is a first-class class (not just a link), with citations to the test names that prove it carries its own evidence, scope, verification status, and can itself be superseded or invalidated.\n- `## Findings` — every defect, missing artifact, or weak test, each with a severity (blocker / major / minor) and the task that owns the fix.\n- `## Verdict` — `APPROVED` / `APPROVED WITH FOLLOW-UPS` / `REJECTED`. A `REJECTED` verdict blocks R26 from starting.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — review file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — spec-alignment section present.\n- `grep -q '## CounterMemory coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — CounterMemory section present per Phase 3 DoD.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — verdict recorded.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists.\n- [ ] Every required section present with concrete content (no placeholder text).\n- [ ] Contract tests added (R26 only) and passing — not applicable to R25.\n- [ ] Verdict declared.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15982,"cache_read_input_tokens":85859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15982,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTEqX34f6x4nqNqXUnhApL","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"91ae2072-94d4-4b21-b2dc-bf052d2415d9","request_id":"req_011Cb7NNhAmfrKHCVCozvQXS","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 2+3+Gate task briefs"}
./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:841:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0158fayGk8TdCJvKN5fwBobH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QuEbpAPeDTAh2At2PyM8AZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T67.md","content":"# T67 — Phase 9 — get_memory_metrics + retrieval relevance surfaces wired through MCP\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T65\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task wires the T65 metrics module through the MCP surface so the `get_memory_metrics` tool from T60 returns the full canonical signal set rather than the fallback session_metrics view, and adds per-call retrieval relevance surfaces (inclusion reasons, scoring breakdowns) into the existing workflow tool responses. Spec §Phase 9 Deliverables names \"retrieval relevance metrics\" as binding, and spec §Phase 4 Definition of Done requires \"workflow tools return memory with inclusion reasons and stable expansion handles … irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" Without this task, the metrics module ships but no MCP client can read it and no per-call relevance signal is exposed.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics.\"\n\n> \"Workflow tools return memory with inclusion reasons and stable expansion handles … irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" (spec §Phase 4 DoD)\n\n> \"The ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode. Compact mode should include only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result.\" (spec §Retrieval Engine)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricScope`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` (T60) — current implementation reading from fallback session_metrics; T67 swaps it to consume `MetricsCollector` directly.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` (T56/T57) — each tool's response carries `MemoryHighlight`s; T67 extends them with per-call relevance scoring.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — MCP tool registration.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — for handle-driven expansion of relevance details.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9, §Retrieval Engine, and §Phase 4 DoD in full.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` as the MCP-facing facade over the T65 `MetricsCollector`. It exposes: (a) `MetricsSurface::collect(scope, signals)` calling the T65 collector and returning `Vec<MetricValue>`; (b) `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call(task_id, tool_name)` returning per-call relevance: per-pivot inclusion score breakdown (graph proximity, semantic similarity, freshness, scope, verification, evidence strength, past usefulness — per spec §Retrieval Engine \"Ranking signals\"), per-memory inclusion reason, excluded high-scoring candidates with rejection reasons; (c) `MetricsSurface::summarize_for_compact_mode(...)` returning a one-line digest suitable for compact tool responses.\n3. Wire `metrics_surface.rs` into `memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` so the tool reads from the T65 collector through this facade rather than the fallback `session_metrics`. The fallback path remains as an explicit `source: SessionMetrics` value when the collector returns `None` for a given signal — never fabricate a value.\n4. Extend the T56/T57 workflow tools' responses to attach per-call relevance via `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call`. In `compact` render mode each `MemoryHighlight` and `Pivot` carries the summarized one-line digest; in `full` / `diagnostic` mode each carries the full score breakdown. Spec §Retrieval Engine: \"The ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode.\"\n5. Add a stable expansion handle (`relevance_detail_handle`) on every `MemoryHighlight` and `Pivot` so `expand_context` can fetch the full diagnostic breakdown without re-running the workflow.\n6. Workspace boundary + scope-leak protections: every `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call` query honors workspace and scope filters, matching the discipline established in T58–T60.\n7. In `metrics_surface_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip the surface's request/response through serde; (b) assert the surface returns every T65 `MetricSignal` variant; (c) assert it returns `null` with a reason when no data is available, never a fabricated value; (d) assert per-call relevance includes every ranking-signal column from spec §Retrieval Engine; (e) assert compact mode digests are bounded in size; (f) assert the diagnostic expansion handle dereferences to the full breakdown; (g) assert workspace boundary and scope filters reject cross-scope queries with a typed error.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` — MCP-facing facade exposing `collect`, `collect_for_call`, `summarize_for_compact_mode`; wires T65 `MetricsCollector` into `get_memory_metrics` (T60) and extends T56/T57 workflow responses with per-call relevance breakdowns and stable expansion handles per spec §Retrieval Engine.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface_tests.rs` — unit tests covering serde round-trip, full signal-set coverage, honest null reporting, per-call relevance breakdown, compact-mode digest bound, expansion-handle dereference, scope-leak rejection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` — confirms the surface file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests` — every metrics-surface test passes (serde round-trip, signal coverage, honest null, per-call breakdown, compact digest bound, expansion-handle dereference, scope-leak rejection).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `MetricsSurface` request/response types reuse `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricScope` from T65; do not introduce parallel types; every public field has a doc comment.\n- No silent error handling — missing data is honest `None` with reason; scope-leak rejections are typed errors.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricsSurface::collect_for_call`, not `MetricsSurface::call_metrics`).\n- For SQLite: storage access flows through T65 collector; no raw SQL in the RPC surface.\n- Observability: surface emits `tracing::info!` spans with `tool`, `scope`, `signal_count`, `source_breakdown` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, `## Retrieval Engine`, `## Phase 4 — Retrieval V1` DoD in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every T65 signal is reachable via `get_memory_metrics`; every T56/T57 workflow response carries per-call relevance + expansion handle in this task — not \"to be added later.\"\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the legacy `session_metrics` view continues to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3897,"cache_read_input_tokens":99814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3897,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"a198de81-caba-4d7a-a742-bf4416702711","request_id":"req_011Cb7NUqgQADaeKzWbKLxf2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:856:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01B3ExiWf97Ku1iLhAq6xya5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fv9dE6NHj9KinQYzsUTtWm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T68.md","content":"# T68 — Phase 9 — Regression dashboard / CLI report\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T65, T66\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships the `lattice_report` binary and its supporting `metrics/report.rs` module so operators and CI can render the full Phase 9 metric set from the T65 collector and the T66 benchmark output. Spec §Phase 9 Deliverables names \"regression dashboard or CLI report\" as binding and the Phase 9 DoD requires that \"changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" The CLI is the surface that turns the metrics module into something a human or CI job can read.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: …regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricScope`, `MetricSource`.\n  - T66 — `golden_anchors.json` and the JSON benchmark report from `cognitive_workspace_benchmark`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/` — current daemon binary location; the new CLI binary lives alongside.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — provides the baseline column for the report.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/` — the canonical metrics module.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`, `## Tests as documentation`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` exposing: (a) `ReportInput { current: Vec<MetricValue>, baseline: Option<Vec<MetricValue>>, benchmark_report_path: PathBuf, scope: MetricScope, success_criteria: SuccessCriteriaThresholds }`; (b) `RegressionReport` rendering per-signal current value, baseline value, delta, target threshold (from spec §Measurable Success Criteria), pass/fail per row; (c) renderers for human-readable text, machine-readable JSON, and a CI-friendly summary line; (d) per-signal evidence pointer back to the contributing event/memory IDs so any regression is investigable. `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` encodes the spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly (30%, 40%, 80%, 0, 0, 90%) so the report's pass/fail column is grounded in the spec.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` as the CLI binary. Argument surface: `--scope`, `--time-range`, `--signals`, `--baseline <path>`, `--benchmark <path>`, `--format text|json|ci-summary`, `--output <path>`, `--fail-on-regression`. The binary loads the current metrics via the T65 collector against the active workspace, optionally loads a baseline JSON, optionally loads the T66 benchmark JSON, and renders the `RegressionReport` to stdout or the `--output` path. With `--fail-on-regression`, exits non-zero when any signal fails its spec §Measurable Success Criteria target.\n4. Author `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` describing: report architecture, signal definitions (referencing T65), thresholds (referencing spec §Measurable Success Criteria), input/output formats, CI integration guidance, regression-investigation runbook. The doc is the operator-facing reference.\n5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` covering: (a) deterministic rendering across all three formats; (b) baseline-vs-current delta computation; (c) target threshold pass/fail logic for each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target; (d) honest reporting of `null` signals (renders as `n/a` with reason, never as zero); (e) exit-code behavior of `--fail-on-regression`; (f) per-signal evidence-pointer round-trip.\n6. Wire the binary into the workspace `Cargo.toml` so `cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` produces an installable binary. Document the build/deploy path in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n7. Workspace boundary: the CLI honors the workspace it was invoked against — it never crosses workspace boundaries even if multiple `.lattice/` paths are reachable.\n8. Honor Cadres coding standard `## Observability`: the CLI emits structured `tracing` output to stderr so CI logs capture every signal collected and every threshold evaluated.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — `lattice_report` CLI binary collecting current metrics, optionally loading baseline + T66 benchmark JSON, rendering the regression report in text/json/ci-summary, exiting non-zero on regression when requested.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` — `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`, three renderers, per-signal evidence pointers; encodes spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` — unit tests covering deterministic rendering, baseline delta, threshold pass/fail, honest null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — operator-facing reference: architecture, signal definitions, thresholds, formats, CI integration, regression runbook.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — confirms the binary entry point exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — confirms the operator doc exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` — the binary compiles cleanly with the rest of the workspace.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::report_tests` — every report test passes (rendering determinism, baseline delta, threshold logic, null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split `report.rs` per renderer if needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; JSON output schema documented in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n- No silent error handling — every IO/parse failure surfaces with a typed error and a non-zero exit code; honest `null` values render as `n/a` with reason, never zero.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`SuccessCriteriaThresholds::memory_inclusion_precision`, not `Thresholds::mip`).\n- For SQLite: storage access goes through T65 `MetricsCollector`; no raw SQL in the binary or report module.\n- Observability: binary emits structured `tracing` to stderr with `scope`, `signal_count`, `pass_count`, `fail_count`, `format` fields per invocation.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` and `## Measurable Success Criteria` in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` and the binary source.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three render formats ship; `--fail-on-regression` is implemented; the operator doc is complete (no \"TBD\" sections).\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the existing `lattice` daemon binary is unaffected.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3269,"cache_read_input_tokens":103711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"279282f3-a4da-48f1-994d-a044bce886f7","request_id":"req_011Cb7NY8HNbB9Meugrxe9qx","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
